; 
; Altscr example config-file   by Paul Spijkerman
;
; Mode in which the program will work.
; Can be anywhere in the config file
; The last mentioned will be used
;
;    /count  -> Uses a counter, so after use a next screen
;               from the row/queue will be used.
;    /random -> Uses a random number to choose screen
;               This mode uses the second counter from the clock
/count

;
; path and filename from file in which the counters will be kept
; if you use multiple cfg files, don't forget to use different names
; Can be anywhere in the config file
;
/countfile
altscr:counter

;
; Path and names of the source screens
; Don't forget to terminate with a #
;
/input
Xbulletins:TCCpc.gr1
Xbulletins:xenobbs.gr1
Xbulletins:PNN.gr1
Xbulletins:local.gr1
#

;
; name and path of the screen you want to change
; This must be a name used by the BBS program
; (not limited to the logout screen)
; Don't forget to backup your old logout.gr1 !!
;
/output
xtext:logout.gr1

;
; Source screens for the next screen, max. 80 in a config file
;
/input
Xbulletins:tccpcr.gr1
Xbulletins:xenobbs.gr1
Xbulletins:top40.gr1
#

/output
xtext:logout.txt
